# KNOWN GAP — `Expr::Index` brackets are NOT a fill-emitted list.
#
# A DISTINCT MECHANISM from the pre-render-above family (its own fixture,
# `fmt_delimited_list_pre_render_above.gg`) and from the fill-emitter
# chokepoint. `v[i]` has exactly one "element" and is emitted with
# HAND-WRITTEN delimiters — `write("[")`, format the index expression,
# `write("]")` — so it never reaches `emit_delimited_list` and there is no
# gate to route it through. Giving it one means either teaching the index
# arm to consult the sideband itself, or generalising the chokepoint to
# single-slot delimited regions.
#
# It is the smallest member of a wider hand-rolled-delimiter family that
# also includes the `write(", ")` comma-loop emitters (pattern field
# lists, tuple and function TYPES, enum tuple-variant field lists,
# meta-construct argument lists) — those are enumerated in `TODO.md`.
#
# CURRENT (measured on the post-chokepoint build):
#     int r = v[0]
#     # SEN index          ← escaped to the enclosing statement indent,
#     print(r)                now a leading comment of `print(r)`
#
# INTENDED (post-fix):
#     int r = v[
#         # SEN index
#         0
#     ]
#
# UN-IGNORE + PROMOTE out of `known_gaps/` when the index brackets gain an
# interior-comment gate.

int main():
    Vector[int] v = [10, 20, 30]
    int r = v[
        # SEN index
        0
    ]
    print(r)
    return 0
